From: Dior Linux maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rtnetlink: allow optional attributes from newer userspace

Modern NetworkManager includes IFA_FLAGS (8) when configuring IPv4 leases.
The legacy common parser rejects it against IFA_MAX (7), preventing the
address from being installed; accepting the DHCP lease then fails to bind
its UDP socket with EADDRNOTAVAIL.

Ignore attributes outside the legacy table without indexing rta_buf. The
message-specific parser still sees the complete message and validates its
known fields and lengths. Keep the existing handler API and buffer layout.

Upstream rationale: 661d2967b3f1b34eeaa7e212e7b9bbe8ee072b59
(rtnetlink: Remove passing of attributes into rtnl_doit functions).
This is a narrow compatibility backport, not the full handler API change.

diff --git a/net/core/rtnetlink.c b/net/core/rtnetlink.c
index 1604bf22..ae2da871 100644
--- a/net/core/rtnetlink.c
+++ b/net/core/rtnetlink.c
@@ -2045,11 +2045,9 @@ static int rtnetlink_rcv_msg(struct sk_buff *skb, struct nlmsghdr *nlh)
 
 		while (RTA_OK(attr, attrlen)) {
 			unsigned flavor = attr->rta_type;
-			if (flavor) {
-				if (flavor > rta_max[sz_idx])
-					return -EINVAL;
+			/* Leave newer attributes to the message-specific parser. */
+			if (flavor && flavor <= rta_max[sz_idx])
 				rta_buf[flavor-1] = attr;
-			}
 			attr = RTA_NEXT(attr, attrlen);
 		}
 	}
